                <pb facs="0544" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg450"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.20/295: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-03T23:00:00-00:44">December 3, 1929—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 3—11 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>69. I have complied with Department’s 49, November 23, 2 p.m. Barclay reticent to
                    comment on nomination but expresses salary high. Will report to the Department
                    by cable any reaction. Barclay asks may Legation’s note be construed as offer of
                    Fiscal Agents toward making any [new?] agreement on salary between the Fiscal
                    Agents and Liberia under article 12, paragraph 3, loan agreement.</p>
                <p>Legation’s understanding salary and allowances fall within article 13, paragraph
                    1.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
